    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Rethinking Teaching is a four day workshop for faculty to examine and develop their thinking about the course design process and their teaching practice. It was held from 25th to 28th July 2017 at AKU's Graduate School of Media and Communication in Nairobi, facilitated by Vivian Neal from Simon Fraser University (Canada) and five of AKU's Teaching and Learning Network staff. Fifteen AKU faculty, mainly from East Africa, attended the workshop.The workshop involved group interaction activities, plus individual focus time for participants to work on the designs of their courses.",
